<title>UK: BRITISH ELECTION DIARY - April 16.</title>
<headline>BRITISH ELECTION DIARY - April 16.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is the election diary for Wednesday April 16:</p>
<p>Prime Minister John Major, Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke, Education Secretary Gillian Shephard and Conservative party chairman Dr Brian Mawhinney will conduct daily press briefing at 0830 GMT.</p>
<p>Major is then due to take off on the campaign trial.</p>
<p>Labour party finance spokesman Gordon Brown, social security spokeswoman Harriet Harman and environmental protection spokesman Michael Meacher hold news conference at 0730 GMT</p>
<p>Splinter anti-European Referendum party holds news conference at 0900 GMT</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 5427947</p>
